                <infoLink name="Exitus Rifle" id="f915-df95-1ece-2078" hidden="false" targetId="5195-1377-ebdf-0847" type="profile"/>
                <infoLink name="Exitus Pistol" id="6cea-41ee-5f54-d5a9" hidden="false" targetId="e146-43f9-0ff4-d037" type="profile"/>
              </infoLinks>
              <profiles>
                <profile name="Spy Mask" id="bdd8-5ec5-5307-32f2" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">The Vindicare&apos;s spy mask reduces the Cover save of his target by 1 (a 6+ save is negated, a 5+ Cover save becomes a 6+ save, and so on). In addition, the spy mask means the Vindicate rolls 2D6x5 for determining how far he can see when the Night Fighting tules are being used.</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
                <profile name="Stealth Suit" id="567d-3342-1313-0857" hidden="false" typeId="456a-26d9-cb27-bd5c" typeName="Wargear">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9e5e-2cfd-7c93-749a">Any unit wishing to shoot at the Vindicate Assassin must test to see if he can be seen using the Night Fighting rules. If the Night Fighting rules are already in use, the Assassin can only be seen if he is within half the normal range of the unit&apos;s vision. (ie, if they score an 18, they can only see the Assassin if he is within 9&quot;).</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
                <profile name="Marksman" id="d4cd-da00-538d-b5a9" hidden="false" typeId="ccb3-7790-3139-7975" typeName="Abilities">
                  <characteristics>
                    <characteristic name="Description" typeId="e24a-6018-20cf-d76c">You may nominate the model targeted by the Vindicate Assassin when he is shooting, such as a Sergeant or a heavy weapons trooper. This means you get to choose which model is taken off, not the enemy. In addition, the Vindicate can target any model in range and line of sight, regardless of any targeting restrictions (such as Independent characters being embedded in a unit).</characteristic>
                  </characteristics>
                </profile>
              </profiles>
            </selectionEntry>
          </selectionEntries>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry name="Death-Cult Assassins" id="33ec-b85b-8f18-43ab" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <infoLinks>
